ight or wrong he's  confident he's as good if not better  than patrick mahomes kyler murray lamar  jackson let me show it  let's not hand off handoff handoff  handoff let me show what i can do while  i still have the skills to do it because  every year he's getting closer and  closer to that point where the  discussion is going to be along the  lines of our current conversations about  drew brees and tom brady all right uh  speaking of a guy who is closer to the  drew brees and tom brady category than  russell wilson when it relates to age  question 11  is this going to be given what the  packers did in the first round of the  draft and the rest of the draft and not  getting help for aaron rodgers but  instead drafting his replacement in  round one trading up to do it is this  going to be in aaron rodgers revenge  tour in 2020  well first of all i hear jordan love has  not looked that great in practice he  struggled  perhaps more than a rookie first round  pick should struggle so i don't know how  much aaron rodgers is currently looking  over his shoulder but we know that he  thrives on motivation and this is  motivation for him he's made that quite  clear the them using the first round  draft pick on jordan love so  aaron rodgers has a chance to do some  really big things this season and i'm  not at all going to be surprised if he's  not in that mvp conversation and perhaps  wins the mvp award at the end of the  season because i do think he's motivated  i do think he thrives on motivation and  chip on his shoulder  yeah i absolutely agree with that in  last year  when the report came out from tyler dunn  of bleacher report about the dysfunction  between rogers and mike mccarthy  one of the observations in the aftermath  of that from ceo mark murphy was maybe  this will be a good thing right  maybe having people upset will will  provide some external motivation and it  worked they went 13-3 and they almost  got to the super bowl and i can't help  but wonder whether 